        <body>
            <trans-unit id="title" resname="title">
                <source>AI Chat</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="understanding.heading" resname="understanding.heading">
                <source>What the AI chat does</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="understanding.text" resname="understanding.text">
                <source>The AI chat answers questions about this TYPO3 installation and prepares changes to pages, content and files. Every change it wants to make waits for your approval. Guided tours walk through a task, such as improving page descriptions, page by page.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="understanding.where.toolbar" resname="understanding.where.toolbar">
                <source>The chat icon in the top bar opens the chat as a panel on every backend page.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="understanding.where.column" resname="understanding.where.column">
                <source>Beside the page module, the chat can sit as a column next to the page tree.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="understanding.where.dashboard" resname="understanding.where.dashboard">
                <source>Dashboard widgets show recent chats, recommendations and start guided tours.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="understanding.where.altTexts" resname="understanding.where.altTexts">
                <source>The list of missing alternative texts offers to write them with the chat.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="action.openChat" resname="action.openChat">
                <source>Open the chat</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="action.chatFullPage" resname="action.chatFullPage">
                <source>The chat as a full page</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="action.altTexts" resname="action.altTexts">
                <source>Missing alternative texts</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.heading" resname="readiness.heading">
                <source>Does it work for you?</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.intro" resname="readiness.intro">
                <source>Each line is checked now, for you, with the rules the chat itself applies. A line marked "Not checked" could not be measured from here.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="column.state" resname="column.state">
                <source>State</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="column.finding" resname="column.finding">
                <source>Finding</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="column.action" resname="column.action">
                <source>What to do</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.access.allowed" resname="readiness.access.allowed">
                <source>You have access to the chat.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.access.noTask" resname="readiness.access.noTask">
                <source>No nr-llm task is configured for the chat, so nobody gets it.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.access.noTaskForYourGroups" resname="readiness.access.noTaskForYourGroups">
                <source>No nr-llm task is configured for your backend groups, and none for everyone else.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.access.notInAllowedGroup" resname="readiness.access.notInAllowedGroup">
                <source>The chat is limited to backend groups you are not a direct member of.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.task.ok" resname="readiness.task.ok">
                <source>Your chat runs the task "%1$s" with the configuration "%2$s".</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.task.missing" resname="readiness.task.missing">
                <source>The nr-llm task %1$d the chat uses for you does not exist.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.task.configurationMissing" resname="readiness.task.configurationMissing">
                <source>The nr-llm task %1$d names no LLM configuration.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.task.configurationDisabled" resname="readiness.task.configurationDisabled">
                <source>The LLM configuration of task %1$d is disabled.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.task.configurationRestricted" resname="readiness.task.configurationRestricted">
                <source>The LLM configuration of task %1$d is restricted to backend groups you are not in.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.tools.ok" resname="readiness.tools.ok">
                <source>The model "%1$s" can call tools, which the chat needs to look things up and prepare changes.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.tools.missing" resname="readiness.tools.missing">
                <source>The model "%1$s" is not marked as able to call tools. The chat can then only answer from the conversation.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.tools.unchecked" resname="readiness.tools.unchecked">
                <source>The configuration "%1$s" chooses its model when it runs, so tool support cannot be checked here.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.unavailableTools.none" resname="readiness.unavailableTools.none">
                <source>No tool of this configuration is withheld from you.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.unavailableTools.some" resname="readiness.unavailableTools.some">
                <source>%1$d tools of this configuration are withheld from you (switched off or not permitted).</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.processing.exec" resname="readiness.processing.exec">
                <source>Each message starts its own background process (processing strategy "exec"); no worker needs to run.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.processing.workerIdle" resname="readiness.processing.workerIdle">
                <source>%1$d workers are waiting for messages right now; %2$d messages are waiting for a worker.</source>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="readiness.processing.noIdleWorker" resname="readiness.processing.noIdleWorker">
                <source>No worker is waiting right now (%1$d messages are waiting). Messages then start a process of their own, which is slower. Workers may be busy or not running; a busy worker leaves no trace.</source>
            </trans-unit>
